---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---
<Page title="Refund Policy — Curfew" stylesheet="style.css">
<Fragment slot="head">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#f5f0e6" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" />
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#16130f" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="images/favicon.png" />
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="images/apple-touch-icon.png" />
</Fragment>
<header class="site-header">
    <nav>
      <a href="/" class="wordmark">Curfew</a>
      <a class="nav-account" href="/account">Open Account</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section>
      <div class="section-inner" style="max-width:640px">
        <h1 class="privacy-heading">Refund Policy</h1>

        <p class="privacy-lede">
          We want you to be happy with Curfew Plus. If it isn't the right fit,
          we offer a straightforward refund.
        </p>

        <h2 class="privacy-section-title">14-day refunds</h2>
        <p class="privacy-prose">
          You can request a full refund within 14 days of your Curfew Plus
          purchase, for any reason. Just email
          <a href="mailto:hello@hypertext.studio">hello@hypertext.studio</a>
          from the address you used at checkout, or include your order number
          from the Stripe receipt. We'll process it promptly.
        </p>

        <h2 class="privacy-section-title">How refunds are issued</h2>
        <p class="privacy-prose">
          Curfew payments are processed by Stripe, so refunds are returned to
          your original payment method through Stripe.
          It can take a few business days for the funds to appear, depending on
          your bank or card issuer.
        </p>

        <h2 class="privacy-section-title">Subscriptions</h2>
        <!-- TODO(legal): confirm the subscription refund/cancellation terms
             below with the owner before launch (proration, mid-period refunds,
             how the 14-day window applies to recurring billing). -->
        <p class="privacy-prose">
          A Curfew Plus subscription renews automatically. You can cancel anytime
          to stop future renewals; Plus stays active until the end of the period
          you have already paid for, then turns off on its own. The 14-day
          window above applies to your most recent charge.
        </p>

        <h2 class="privacy-section-title">About your license key</h2>
        <p class="privacy-prose">
          One-time Curfew Plus keys are perpetual and verified offline. Because
          they are not remotely revocable, a refunded one-time key may
          technically continue to unlock Plus on your machines; requesting a
          refund is your agreement to stop using Curfew Plus and delete the key,
          and we trust you to honor that. Subscription keys carry an expiry and
          are refreshed online while active, so they stop unlocking Plus on their
          own once a subscription ends.
        </p>

        <h2 class="privacy-section-title">After 14 days</h2>
        <p class="privacy-prose">
          Beyond the 14-day window we generally can't offer refunds, but if
          something has gone wrong, reach out anyway —
          <a href="mailto:hello@hypertext.studio">hello@hypertext.studio</a> —
          and we'll do our best to make it right.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>
      Made by <a href="https://hypertext.studio">Hypertext Studio</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="docs.html">MCP setup</a> ·
      <a href="terms.html">Terms</a> ·
      <a href="refund.html">Refund</a> ·
      <a href="security.html">Security</a> ·
      <a href="retention.html">Retention</a> ·
      <a href="privacy.html">Privacy</a>
    </p>
  </footer>
</Page>
